<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Data Creation</h2>

<figure id="A1.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>List of our tasks, showing <math id="A1.T2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A1.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(x))</annotation></semantics></math> for the random example in <a href="#S2.T1" title="In Limitations ‣ 2 Task Setup ‣ How Do Language Models Compose Functions?" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. Tasks with neither <math id="A1.T2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(x)</annotation></semantics></math> nor <math id="A1.T2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(x))</annotation></semantics></math> are omitted. <math id="A1.T2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(g(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(g(x))</annotation></semantics></math> only shown if distinct from <math id="A1.T2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(f(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(f(x))</annotation></semantics></math>.</figcaption>
<div id="A1.T2.2" class="ltx_logical-block">
        
<div id="A1.T2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center">
<div id="A1.T2.p1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:517.1pt;height:121.2pt;vertical-align:-58.1pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(0.0pt,0.0pt) scale(1,1) ;">
<p id="A1.T2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.T2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text">
<span id="A1.T2.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<span class="ltx_thead">
<span id="A1.T2.p1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
